"""Set L labels (round 27), written by hand from the official pages in pages/ before any extractor ran on set L.

Set L is the frozen test set for the round-27 rules: the rules were fixed on set K and the development sets, the code
was committed (02e3394, 4ee4233) before any set-L page was fetched, and nothing on set L was used to change a rule.
Labels follow the round-27 reading of a page:
  nationality   "any" only when the page states that every nationality may apply; "international students",
                "UK and international", fee status, domicile, a region without a list, or an invitation ("students
                from around the world") is "not_stated"; "outside the EU/EEA (and Switzerland)" lists those countries
  funding_class what the page proves: fully_funded needs tuition and living costs both covered; a stated discount,
                share or cap is partially_funded; a page that names no component is "not_stated"
  cycle_status  open / upcoming / closed / not_announced / rolling / expected / not_stated on 2026-10-18
  deadlines     applicant deadline dates stated with a year for this programme (not other steps, not other awards)
Close calls are marked "ambiguous"; the report gives results with and without them.
Run once to write labels.json; manifest.json then freezes it."""
